# Optional: GitHub Personal Access Token
# Without a token the app uses the public GitHub API (60 req/h per IP).
# With a token the limit is 5000 req/h and private repos become accessible.
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Required scopes: repo (for private repos) or no scopes for public repos.
#
# For Vercel: add this as an Environment Variable in your project settings.
# VITE_ prefix is required so Vite exposes it to the browser bundle.
VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Anthropic / Claude ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two independent ways to use Claude in the desktop app:
#
#   • "Claude" provider — calls the Anthropic API directly. Needs a real API key
#     (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, `sk-ant-api03-…`). Set it in your shell before launch.
#
#   • "Claude Code" provider — drives the local `claude` CLI as a subprocess, so
#     it works with a Claude Code OAuth token (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN,
#     `sk-ant-oat…`, ~1y, minted via `claude setup-token`) OR a normal API key.
#     Requires the `claude` binary on PATH. No direct-API / CORS restrictions
#     apply because Claude Code makes the requests, not the browser.
#
# These are read from the process environment on desktop (not VITE_-prefixed).
